WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:15.073
Jason couldn't concentrate.

2
00:00:15.074 --> 00:00:17.218
He couldn't even walk.

3
00:00:17.219 --> 00:00:20.045
His legs were so itchy!

4
00:00:20.046 --> 00:00:24.389
Last night he and his dad had eaten dinner outside.

5
00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:29.774
By the time they went inside, Jason was covered in mosquito bites.

6
00:00:29.775 --> 00:00:34.058
Itchy, horrible mosquito bites.

7
00:00:34.059 --> 00:00:36.626
"I can't take it anymore!"

8
00:00:36.627 --> 00:00:40.624
Jason showed everyone the red spots on his legs.

9
00:00:40.625 --> 00:00:45.654
"Wow," said Nina. "They look itchy."

10
00:00:45.655 --> 00:00:50.012
"You should have used bug spray," said Izzie.

11
00:00:50.013 --> 00:00:53.693
"I can't use bug spray," Jason said.

12
00:00:53.694 --> 00:00:56.548
"Why not?" Nina asked.

13
00:00:56.549 --> 00:01:01.215
"Because I'm allergic to the chemicals." Jason frowned.

14
00:01:01.216 --> 00:01:05.993
"Well then it's your lucky day!" said Mr. Dunn.

15
00:01:05.994 --> 00:01:11.949
"Lucky?" Jason echoed. "What's lucky about mosquito bites?"

16
00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:17.171
"We're making Campers' Bug Spray today," Mr. Dunn explained.

17
00:01:17.172 --> 00:01:20.269
"It's all-natural bug spray."

18
00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:23.241
"Really?" Jason didn't believe it.

19
00:01:23.242 --> 00:01:25.370
"How do you make it?"

20
00:01:25.371 --> 00:01:28.859
"Mr. Dunn is a chemistry teacher.

21
00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.472
So he can explain what to do.

22
00:01:31.473 --> 00:01:33.974
Right, Mr. Dunn?"

23
00:01:33.975 --> 00:01:36.469
Bobby looked at his teacher.

24
00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:39.662
"That's the plan." Mr. Dunn nodded.

25
00:01:39.663 --> 00:01:47.780
"Have a seat."

26
00:01:47.781 --> 00:01:54.233
"In some of these bottles are very strong oils called essential oils.

27
00:01:54.234 --> 00:02:01.453
By mixing certain essential oils, you can make a scent that will send mosquitoes running."

28
00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:04.784
Mr. Dunn coughed.

29
00:02:04.785 --> 00:02:07.040
"I mean, flying."

30
00:02:07.041 --> 00:02:12.139
Nina giggled. She liked Mr. Dunn's silly jokes.

31
00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:16.699
"But won't the scent make us want to run away too?" Ethan asked.

32
00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.873
"I don't think so.

33
00:02:18.874 --> 00:02:23.696
But you can decide for yourself in a minute," Mr. Dunn said.

34
00:02:23.697 --> 00:02:28.875
"Everyone, take one of the spray bottles and write your name on it.

35
00:02:28.876 --> 00:02:34.902
This will be your bug spray bottle."

36
00:02:34.903 --> 00:02:39.154
Jason carefully wrote his name on a bottle.

37
00:02:39.155 --> 00:02:46.612
"First we have to add what's called a base oil," said Mr. Dunn.

38
00:02:46.613 --> 00:02:49.977
"Today our base is olive oil.

39
00:02:49.978 --> 00:02:55.019
We'll start with that so the essential oils aren't so strong."

40
00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:58.594
"And so we won't be allergic?" Jason asked.

41
00:02:58.595 --> 00:03:06.387
"Yes. Some people get a rash from too much strong essential oil," Mr. Dunn said.

42
00:03:06.388 --> 00:03:10.662
"So we're going to carefully measure how much we put in."

43
00:03:10.663 --> 00:03:16.169
Everyone poured in the olive oil.

44
00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:19.220
Next Mr. Dunn held up a bottle.

45
00:03:19.221 --> 00:03:21.940
"See this bottle's special top?

46
00:03:21.941 --> 00:03:27.578
The dropper helps us measure the eucalyptus oil one drop at a time."

47
00:03:27.579 --> 00:03:31.214
Mr. Dunn put a few drops in his hand.

48
00:03:31.215 --> 00:03:38.059
Then he rubbed his hands together and held them up for the kids to smell.

49
00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:40.621
"I like it," Izzie said.

50
00:03:40.622 --> 00:03:42.933
"It smells clean and fresh."

51
00:03:42.934 --> 00:03:45.218
Ethan took a sniff.

52
00:03:45.219 --> 00:03:48.967
"Wow! That's strong."

53
00:03:48.968 --> 00:03:54.220
"Put twenty drops into your bottle," Mr. Dunn said.

54
00:03:54.221 --> 00:04:00.292
Jason squinted. "I feel like it might sting my eyes," he said.

55
00:04:00.293 --> 00:04:04.565
"The oil could sting your eyes!" Mr. Dunn said.

56
00:04:04.566 --> 00:04:11.228
"So be very careful not to touch your eyes after handling essential oils."

57
00:04:11.229 --> 00:04:14.874
"What do we put in next?" Bobby asked.

58
00:04:14.875 --> 00:04:17.779
Mr. Dunn held up another bottle.

59
00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:20.711
"Citronella essential oil."

60
00:04:20.712 --> 00:04:25.505
"We have citronella candles in our backyard," Nina said.

61
00:04:25.506 --> 00:04:31.701
"Citronella keeps mosquitoes away," Mr. Dunn said.

62
00:04:31.702 --> 00:04:36.383
"So add twenty drops of this too.

63
00:04:36.384 --> 00:04:39.582
Shake it up and you're done!

64
00:04:39.583 --> 00:04:45.129
Next time we go on a hike, you can spray it on your arms and legs.

65
00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:48.611
Try this if you go outside tonight, Jason.

66
00:04:48.612 --> 00:04:53.359
I don't think any mosquitoes will bother you," Mr. Dunn said.

67
00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:56.871
"I'll try it," Jason said.

68
00:04:56.872 --> 00:05:07.657
"But after last night, I have no skin left to bite anyway!"

69
00:05:07.658 --> 00:05:19.419
[caption_out@
